{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "John in Brazil", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Bright Future", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Nature Around Us > Rainforest", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Making and Responding to Suggestions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Making Suggestions</span><br>  <br>You use modals when you want to give suggestions. </br><span class=\"strong\">Might</span> is often used with <span class=\"strong\">want</span> to give suggestions.<br>  <br>Examples:<br>  <br><span class=\"italic\">You might want to look at the ingredients in your shampoo.<br> You might want to grab your umbrella.</span><br>   <br>You can use the word, <span class=\"strong\">Let's </span> with a verb to make a suggestion.<br> Let's is the short form of Let us. <br>  <br>Examples:<br> <span class=\"italic\"> Let's go to the park. The weather is great!<br></span>  <br>You can also use Wh- questions:<br>  <br>Why don't you \u2026 ?<br>  How about \u2026 ?<br>  <br>Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\">Why don't you study at the library?<br> How about studying at the park?<br></span>   <span class=\"strong\"><br>Responding to Suggestions<br></span>  <br>You can accept suggestions by saying:<br>  <span class=\"italic\"><br>Yes, I'd like to.<br> Yes, I'd love to.<br> What a good idea!<br> Why not?<br></span>   <br>You can refuse suggestions by saying:<br> <br><span class=\"italic\">No, let's not.<br> No, I'd rather not.<br> I don't feel like it.<br></span>", "type": "describer"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Cause and Effect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use expressions like  <span class=\"italic\">because</span>, <span class=\"italic\">since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">owing to</span>, and  <span class=\"italic\">due to</span> to talk about the results of  a certain cause.<br>   <br>>Examples: <span class=\"italic\"><br>We went for a jog in the park  <span class=\"strong\">because</span> it was such a nice day.<br> The doctor refused to discharge the patient  <span class=\"strong\">since</span> his test results were unclear.<br> She can't read the letter <span class=\"strong\">as</span> she is not fluent in Mandarin.<br> He can't join the group <span class=\"strong\">for</span> he has an appointment.<br> <span class=\"strong\">Owing to</span> his knowledge of weather patterns, he knew rain was coming.<br> <span class=\"strong\">Due to</span> the bad weather, they didn't go on the hiking trip.<br> </span>  <br>You can also say:<br> <ul><li>The cause of \u2026 is \u2026</li> <li>\u2026 is caused by / is due to \u2026</li> <li>Thanks to ...</li></ul>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The cause of global warming is pollution.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Global warming is caused by/is due to pollution.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Thanks to global warming, the seas are rising.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "way of life ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a typical way in which a person or group lives ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They had to change their way of life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to  talk about ecological issues.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "chemical", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a substance that is made by a chemical process", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are chemicals in our food.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "artificial", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not natural or real ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are no artificial ingredients in the soap.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "shipment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a load of goods sent to a customer or store ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are sending out a big shipment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to carry", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have something ready to be sold ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How many products do you carry?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "impact ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a powerful or major influence or effect ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cutting down the trees had a negative impact on the community.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "deforestation  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the cutting down or burning of all the trees in an area", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is a lot of deforestation happening in the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "public", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the people of a country ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We decided to create our own products and sell them to the public.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "warehouse", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large building used for storing goods ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The products are stored in the warehouse.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn4le06ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Write one positive and one negative effect for each cause below.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use your imagination, and write complete sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your answers with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the sentences aloud.<br/> <br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Because the smell of the shampoo was very strong, ...</span><br/>_________________________________&nbsp;/<br/>__________________________________</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Because John missed the tour bus in Costa Rica, ...</span><br/>__________________________________&nbsp;/<br/>__________________________________</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Because&nbsp;Vanessa&nbsp;went&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;long&nbsp;walk&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;beach&nbsp;in&nbsp;Mexico,&nbsp;...</span><br/>__________________________________&nbsp;/&nbsp;__________________________________</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Because&nbsp;Peter&nbsp;went&nbsp;out&nbsp;for&nbsp;dinner&nbsp;with&nbsp;friends&nbsp;from&nbsp;work,&nbsp;...</span><br/>__________________________________&nbsp;/&nbsp;__________________________________</li></ul>", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write sentences using cause and effect to describe situations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice speaking by saying the sentences to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use my imagination to talk about situations in other countries.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn4le06ob08re2img04.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn4le06ob08re2img04.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-100\">Staff member</span>: Jim, I would like you to meet our tour group. Why don't you tell them about your project?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jim</span>: Yes, I'd like to. We made changes to our lifestyle because of the negative impact of deforestation.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Staff member</span>: Are you saying that due to the cutting down of trees in your area, your community changed their way of life?<br>"}, {"image": "engenn4le06ob08re2img01.jpg", "time": "21500", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-100\">Jim</span>: Exactly. We had a lot of animals, but since many areas turned to desert, we cannot feed them anymore."}, {"image": "engenn4le06ob08re2img05.jpg", "time": "30000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-100\">Staff member</span>: Tell us about the project, Jim.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jim</span>: We knew that rainforest plants were good for our skin and hair. We decided to create our own products and sell them to the public.<br>"}, {"image": "engenn4le06ob08re2img03.jpg", "time": "42000", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-100\">Staff member</span>: What a fantastic idea! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jim</span>: Our products are all natural, with no chemicals or artificial ingredients. Plus, they have an exotic smell. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Staff</span>: How many products do you carry?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jim</span>: We currently have four - shampoo, conditioner, soap and face cream.<br>"}, {"image": "engenn4le06ob08re2img04.jpg", "time": "62000", "id": 5, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-100\">Staff member</span>: Your community now has a bright future.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jim</span>: We do. How about your group stops by our warehouse tomorrow? We are sending out a big shipment.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Staff member</span>: We'd love to. Thanks for the invitation.<br>"}], "audiosrc": "engenn4le06ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le06ob08re2img04.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "", "time": "5000", "id": 1, "text": "<span class = \"bullet\"</span>What is cause and effect?</span>"}, {"image": "", "time": "18000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class = \"bullet\">Example sentences that use conjunctions</span>"}, {"image": "", "time": "92000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class = \"bullet\">Things to remember</span>"}], "video_src": "engenn4le06ob08re3vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "I can write about ecological issues.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can write about causes, effects and solutions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can ask and respond to suggestions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What kind of shampoo, conditioner and soap do you use?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Is it important for them to have natural ingredients? Why or Why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask a partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Writing Spot: Wash your hair with our exquisite Rainforest Shampoo. The exotic smell  brings the Rainforest to life!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Listen to the conversation between a member of Amazon Orientation and Jim, the leader of a  community living  in the Amazon rainforest.", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"co